WEBVTT

00:01.840 --> 00:07.560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:07.560 --> 00:12.980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:19.540 --> 00:22.860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:22.860 --> 00:25.540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:25.540 --> 00:31.840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

00:31.840 --> 00:37.960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

00:37.960 --> 00:44.040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:44.180 --> 00:50.200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

00:50.340 --> 00:57.080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

00:57.260 --> 01:02.620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

01:02.840 --> 01:09.340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

01:09.340 --> 01:15.100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

01:15.100 --> 01:21.300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

01:21.300 --> 01:28.120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

01:28.120 --> 01:30.940

01:31.080 --> 01:32.820
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

01:32.820 --> 01:34.240
Hello, Edward.

01:34.860 --> 01:36.820
You appear to have grown some.

01:38.520 --> 01:40.420
I spoke with Pinako.

01:41.520 --> 01:44.300
- You tried human transmutation.
- [GASP]

01:45.380 --> 01:48.080
What makes you think
you can show up like this?

01:48.200 --> 01:50.800
There's nothing left
for you here anymore!

01:51.920 --> 01:53.580
I noticed.

01:54.000 --> 01:55.640
Tell me, Edward...

01:55.680 --> 01:58.300
what possessed you
to burn down my home?

01:59.540 --> 02:02.500
After what happened
we vowed to never turn back.

02:02.500 --> 02:05.920
- We did it as a symbol of our resolve.
- No you didn't.

02:06.600 --> 02:08.540
- You were hiding the memory.
- [GASP]

02:09.740 --> 02:12.880
You didn't want to be reminded
of what you've done,

02:12.920 --> 02:16.760
and thought you could erase the
memory by destroying the evidence.

02:18.180 --> 02:19.800
You're wrong!

02:19.840 --> 02:23.680
It's just like a child who hides
the sheets after he wets the bed.

02:24.480 --> 02:26.720
You ran away, and you know it.

02:26.800 --> 02:27.780
[SHUDDERING GASP]

02:30.040 --> 02:31.020
I...

02:31.260 --> 02:33.020
You don't know a damn thing!

02:33.060 --> 02:36.300
You make me sick to my stomach.

02:38.040 --> 02:41.960
He's exactly like I was when I was his age.

02:50.020 --> 02:52.220
[DOOR OPENS]

02:55.540 --> 02:59.540
[YOUNG ED AND AL LAUGHING]

03:16.960 --> 03:18.560
[DOOR CLOSES]

03:21.320 --> 03:25.960
[LOW GROWLING]

03:25.960 --> 03:28.260
PINAKO: You haven't changed
in the slightest.

03:28.480 --> 03:30.540
All these years...

03:30.540 --> 03:33.300
and you look exactly the same.
[CHUCKLES]

03:34.980 --> 03:38.340
Where have you been all this time?
Why didn't you come back sooner?

03:38.640 --> 03:41.080
Tricia was waiting for you
until the very end.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.100
- Pinako
- Hm?

03:52.560 --> 03:55.340
The life form my sons transmuted...

03:56.080 --> 03:59.320
- are you positive that it was Tricia?
- Huh?

04:00.560 --> 04:02.040
Well, I wouldn't...

04:02.300 --> 04:04.840
it didn't even look human to me...

04:04.840 --> 04:08.140
- so I wouldn't think of it as—
- No. That's not what I'm asking.

04:09.260 --> 04:12.780
Did you notice the eye color,
or the hair color?

04:12.880 --> 04:13.420
Huh?

04:15.640 --> 04:17.200
What are you trying to get at?

04:17.560 --> 04:20.160
Are you telling me that
that wasn't even Tricia?

04:22.300 --> 04:24.660
For all that those boys sacrificed...

04:24.680 --> 04:28.160
you're saying that thing they created
wasn't even their mother?

04:29.880 --> 04:33.760
LING: Whoa, you don't sleep or eat? 
You don't even run out of breath?

04:34.160 --> 04:37.260
AL: Uh-huh, I just have to make
sure the seal doesn't get harmed.

04:37.580 --> 04:38.900
That's so cool!

04:39.000 --> 04:40.920
So you really are immortal then, huh?

04:41.840 --> 04:43.160
- No, I'm not.
-[GASPS]

04:43.880 --> 04:46.500
This body, it's like a time bomb.

04:47.700 --> 04:49.280
Barry mentioned something,

04:49.400 --> 04:53.920
and it made me realize that any type of body
is incompatible with a foreign soul.

04:54.100 --> 04:58.000
Pairing them together,
the body will eventually reject it.

04:58.000 --> 04:58.580
[GASP]

04:58.960 --> 05:04.340
It could happen tomorrow, or ten years
from now, but it's inevitable that it will.

05:04.720 --> 05:05.780
Oh no!

05:06.020 --> 05:08.640
Al, we've got to get you
back in your regular body!

05:08.660 --> 05:10.000
LING: Well, hold on.

05:10.280 --> 05:12.440
If it's about to give out on you...

05:12.480 --> 05:15.720
couldn't you just transfer your soul
into some other object?

05:16.520 --> 05:18.060
Because if that's the case...

05:18.080 --> 05:19.640
then for the time being...

05:19.660 --> 05:22.660
well you're impervious to pain,
and you don't have to eat!

05:23.480 --> 05:25.480
It sounds like a great deal to me!

05:25.500 --> 05:26.540
No it isn't!

05:26.840 --> 05:28.840
You don't know what you're talking about!

05:32.340 --> 05:33.280
Sorry.

05:34.140 --> 05:35.480
Winry?!

05:35.940 --> 05:37.120
[DOOR CLOSES]

05:44.200 --> 05:45.500
[KNOCKING]

05:45.540 --> 05:48.100
AL: Winry?
I'm coming in.

05:55.020 --> 05:59.160
You know, you and brother
always gotta be the first to explode.

05:59.200 --> 06:02.040
I never get the chance
to be the one to get mad.

06:04.060 --> 06:06.120
It's just... Well...

06:10.200 --> 06:12.200
I guess I can't fall asleep.

06:12.300 --> 06:14.280
I don't think this body will let me.

06:15.580 --> 06:16.680
Oh.

06:24.580 --> 06:27.160
Just tell me you're going
to get your body back.

06:27.740 --> 06:28.900
Okay?

06:29.640 --> 06:30.840
[AL GASPS]

06:34.940 --> 06:35.860
ED: Give it back!

06:35.880 --> 06:38.180
You have to give my brother his body back!

06:38.200 --> 06:40.080
He's the only family I have!

06:40.120 --> 06:42.240
I won't let you take it!

06:42.260 --> 06:43.220
Take it?

06:43.240 --> 06:45.660
- [ED GASPS]
- Do you even know what you're saying?

06:45.680 --> 06:49.100
You're the one who tossed his body aside
and put him in that armor.

06:49.140 --> 06:51.460
- Aren't you, Alchemist?
-[ED GASPS]

06:51.700 --> 06:53.060
It's true.

06:53.900 --> 06:56.220
You and I are exactly the same.

06:56.280 --> 06:58.080
Accept it, Edward.

06:58.920 --> 07:00.760
- We make monsters.

07:00.840 --> 07:02.100
[GASP]

07:03.740 --> 07:04.980
[DISORTED VOICE] Edward...

07:04.980 --> 07:08.180
Why did you leave me here like this?

07:08.180 --> 07:10.180
[SHUDDERING GASP]

07:11.100 --> 07:13.660
PINAKO: Ed? Get out of bed already!

07:13.660 --> 07:15.620
Your father's about to head out!

07:16.640 --> 07:19.040
[WHIMPERING]

07:21.580 --> 07:22.520
This one.

07:22.520 --> 07:24.040
Do you mind if I keep it?

07:24.740 --> 07:27.660
It's the only photo we had
taken with all four of us.

07:27.940 --> 07:29.560
Of course. You're welcome to it.

07:29.620 --> 07:30.660
Thank you.

07:33.800 --> 07:36.240
I need to tell you
something important, Pinako.

07:36.520 --> 07:37.560
Huh?

07:37.560 --> 07:38.800
[DOOR OPENS]

07:40.440 --> 07:43.620
Something terrible is going
to happen in this country soon.

07:43.880 --> 07:45.780
You should escape while you can.

07:45.860 --> 07:46.800
[SCOFFS]

07:46.840 --> 07:49.540
This country's lousy with terrible things.

07:49.820 --> 07:51.380
And I can't leave.

07:51.460 --> 07:54.940
I've got other people who need me
here in case they want to come home.

07:56.820 --> 07:58.680
I've given you my warning.

08:01.340 --> 08:02.980
Hey, Hohenheim, wait!

08:03.720 --> 08:06.260
Try not to be such a stranger, all right?

08:11.520 --> 08:13.600
I wish I could, Pinako.

08:13.680 --> 08:16.980
It's too bad I won't get to
enjoy your cooking anymore.

08:20.760 --> 08:25.900
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

08:40.340 --> 08:43.780
You're not really gonna dig it up,
are you, Ed?

08:43.900 --> 08:46.700
[SHOVEL CLANGS, ED GRUNTS]

08:49.680 --> 08:51.160
Why don't we go back?

08:51.540 --> 08:52.840
No.

08:53.360 --> 08:55.520
My stumps are aching from the weather.

08:55.640 --> 08:57.000
It's about to rain.

08:57.540 --> 08:59.140
Let's just hurry and do this.

09:14.280 --> 09:16.160
[ED GAGGING]

09:18.380 --> 09:19.560
Ed!

09:20.000 --> 09:22.000
Don't push yourself.

09:22.880 --> 09:26.000
[SHUDDERING AND GROANING]

09:29.000 --> 09:30.900
Let's head on home.

09:31.440 --> 09:32.440
No.

09:32.440 --> 09:34.240
[SHUDDERS]

09:34.240 --> 09:37.760
I'm not gonna be able to move
forward until I know for sure.

09:38.240 --> 09:39.560
Besides...

09:39.600 --> 09:41.000
You ran away.

09:41.340 --> 09:43.200
I won't run away from this.

10:22.480 --> 10:24.020
[SHOVEL HITS BONE]

10:35.880 --> 10:36.920
[GASPS]

10:40.020 --> 10:41.000
Granny...

10:41.800 --> 10:45.000
Mom's hair was a light chestnut color...

10:46.680 --> 10:48.080
This is black.

10:50.840 --> 10:53.320
This femur, it's much too long.

10:55.220 --> 10:58.680
And this pelvis, I'm pretty sure it's male.

10:58.820 --> 10:59.680
It is?

11:01.420 --> 11:05.120
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
this isn't your mother, Ed.

11:07.960 --> 11:09.440
[ED WHIMPERS]

11:14.720 --> 11:22.380
[LAUGHING]

11:24.220 --> 11:25.460
And that's it.

11:25.820 --> 11:28.540
It really is impossible to
bring the dead back to life.

11:29.260 --> 11:31.160
The undeniable truth.

11:31.920 --> 11:35.780
[LAUGHS]
It was impossible all along

11:38.180 --> 11:40.260
Edward, now listen to me.

11:40.300 --> 11:42.440
You've gotta get a hold of yourself.

11:44.160 --> 11:45.280
[SIGH]

11:45.560 --> 11:47.680
I'm okay, Granny. It's okay.

11:48.740 --> 11:52.380
From the moment I made this
thing, it's been a symbol of my despair.

11:53.040 --> 11:54.260
But not anymore.

11:54.640 --> 11:56.440
Now it's an emblem of hope.

11:58.060 --> 12:00.200
Al can be returned to normal!

12:01.440 --> 12:03.300
Fullmetal Alchemist.

12:04.360 --> 12:06.420
Fullmetal Alchemist.

12:18.420 --> 12:24.300
[PHONE RINGING]

12:25.260 --> 12:27.100
Curtis residence.

12:27.220 --> 12:28.720
I didn't expect this.

12:28.760 --> 12:30.040
You never call.

12:30.380 --> 12:31.440
Uh, yeah.

12:31.720 --> 12:34.000
I need to ask you something, teacher.

12:34.360 --> 12:35.440
But, well...

12:37.160 --> 12:38.320
Well what?

12:38.760 --> 12:39.860
Spit it out.

12:42.740 --> 12:45.620
It has to do with when you
tried to transmute your baby.

12:45.620 --> 12:46.780
[GASP]

12:49.200 --> 12:50.720
What about it, Ed?

12:51.220 --> 12:54.740
The thing is... What Al and I transmuted...

12:55.000 --> 12:56.840
It wasn't actually our mother.

12:58.600 --> 13:00.220
What is this, Ed?

13:00.220 --> 13:01.940
What are you trying to tell me?

13:02.500 --> 13:05.900
I'm sorry to ask you this,
but the child you transmuted...

13:06.300 --> 13:09.720
Are you sure that it was your
child that you brought back?

13:11.380 --> 13:12.580
[GASP]

13:12.580 --> 13:14.580
[PHONE HANGS UP]

13:22.620 --> 13:23.860
PINAKO: Thank you, Ed.

13:24.960 --> 13:28.040
It's good to know my son
and his wife helped people.

13:29.500 --> 13:31.360
I'm proud of them.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.640
So Hohenheim...

13:41.660 --> 13:43.900
Did he even bother to say where he was going?

13:44.160 --> 13:45.720
Of course he didn't.

13:45.740 --> 13:46.640
And I didn't a—

13:46.640 --> 13:47.840
Ahh!

13:47.880 --> 13:49.280
What's wrong with me?

13:49.380 --> 13:52.080
I can't believe I forgot
to give him the message!

13:52.460 --> 13:53.580
A message?

13:53.820 --> 13:54.600
Yes.

13:55.060 --> 13:57.960
A last request...
From your mother.

13:59.440 --> 14:01.400
I'll be gone when he returns.

14:02.280 --> 14:04.040
Can you tell him something?

14:05.160 --> 14:08.300
I need him to know... I
couldn't keep my promise.

14:08.740 --> 14:10.220
I died before he did.

14:10.420 --> 14:12.280
And I'm so sorry.

14:13.480 --> 14:14.660
Promise?

14:14.700 --> 14:15.460
What promise?

14:15.480 --> 14:16.920
You got me.

14:17.420 --> 14:20.620
Sorry to ask, but could you
pass it on if you bump into him?

14:20.780 --> 14:22.440
Why should I have to?

14:22.520 --> 14:26.960
I know it doesn't seem like it,
but he does care about you and your brother.

14:27.000 --> 14:28.100
[LAUGHS]

14:28.100 --> 14:31.400
Yeah, I'll pass it on right
after I clock him in the face.

14:31.400 --> 14:33.400
[TRAIN HORN]

14:34.200 --> 14:36.660
Heading back to Central
already, are you?

14:36.680 --> 14:42.620
Yeah. Al's probably mad at me.
I'm gonna have plenty of explaining to do.

14:46.380 --> 14:49.340
What the hell?!

14:49.380 --> 14:51.140
I'm sorry, brother!

14:51.440 --> 14:54.240
Wha—how are you this beat up?!

14:55.760 --> 14:57.000
And you!

14:57.000 --> 14:59.120
What the hell are you doing here?!

14:59.180 --> 15:00.760
Eating a delicious dinner.

15:00.760 --> 15:02.000
[DOOR OPENS]

15:03.040 --> 15:04.120
Seriously!

15:04.140 --> 15:05.920
How did this happen to you?!

15:05.920 --> 15:06.940
Uh...

15:08.800 --> 15:11.160
ED: A Homunculus
and Barry the Chopper...

15:11.180 --> 15:15.380
And just to throw a cherry on top,
you find out your body might reject your soul.

15:17.640 --> 15:20.940
I'm gonna have to extend what
little you have left of your armor.

15:28.000 --> 15:29.060
[SIGHS]

15:33.600 --> 15:36.700
Ed, he'll be able to get
his body back, right?

15:36.720 --> 15:38.160
Yeah, of course he will.

15:38.160 --> 15:40.420
I told you I'm gonna get it back.

15:44.100 --> 15:45.460
Al...

15:46.300 --> 15:47.980
I've gotta tell you something.

15:48.000 --> 15:50.900
I dug up the body that we
transmuted in Resembool.

15:50.900 --> 15:51.000
[AL GASPS]

15:53.680 --> 15:54.860
What?!

15:54.860 --> 15:56.240
Why would you do that?!

15:56.260 --> 15:57.460
Because, Al...

15:57.960 --> 16:01.220
I found out that the thing we buried
wasn't really our mother.

16:02.480 --> 16:03.740
[GASP]

16:05.280 --> 16:07.740
But... Hold on a minute.

16:07.740 --> 16:09.120
The thing we made?
Then that means...

16:09.120 --> 16:10.620
The thing we made?

16:10.640 --> 16:13.300
I don't know what,
but it was something completely different.

16:13.380 --> 16:16.100
But if it wasn't, then what happened to me?

16:16.100 --> 16:17.200
That's just it.

16:17.200 --> 16:20.180
This has actually convinced
me we can return you to normal.

16:20.280 --> 16:20.960
[AL GASPS]

16:21.000 --> 16:22.060
Ed, are you sure?

16:22.080 --> 16:22.880
Yeah.

16:23.260 --> 16:26.180
But before I start explaining how...

16:26.180 --> 16:29.880
Well, uh, Winry... Do, um... Uh...

16:29.880 --> 16:33.800
Do you remember when Al and I got in a fight
when we were kids about...

16:33.840 --> 16:35.000
Who'd marry you?

16:35.020 --> 16:35.780
Huh?

16:36.040 --> 16:38.100
The fight we were
talking about on the roof?

16:38.300 --> 16:39.280
Yeah, that one.

16:39.300 --> 16:41.300
Al told me you turned him down.

16:41.300 --> 16:42.020
Mm-hmm.

16:42.020 --> 16:43.200
Turned you both down.

16:43.300 --> 16:44.200
Whatever.

16:44.200 --> 16:46.040
So the question's for both of you, then.

16:46.040 --> 16:47.700
What was your reasoning?

16:48.220 --> 16:49.740
She said...

16:50.340 --> 16:52.760
[BOTH]: "I just don't like
men who are shorter than me."

16:52.760 --> 16:54.760
[ED SCREAMS]

16:56.160 --> 16:58.960
You can't judge a man
for something he can't help!

16:58.980 --> 17:00.020
WINRY: Uh...
ED: [WAILING]

17:00.020 --> 17:03.760
WINRY: I don't really see how this has anything to do with getting Al's body back.
ED: [CONTINUES WAILING]

17:03.920 --> 17:05.460
I had to be sure.

17:05.480 --> 17:08.200
Al had a memory of
something I don't recall.

17:08.260 --> 17:11.160
And you seem to clearly
remember it the same way, Winry.

17:11.440 --> 17:13.760
Which means that it
happened without a doubt.

17:13.920 --> 17:16.540
So now that we know you
remembered something real,

17:16.560 --> 17:20.500
then we also know for a fact
that really is Al bonded in there.

17:21.720 --> 17:23.100
I pulled you out, Al.

17:23.260 --> 17:24.800
I actually did it.

17:25.180 --> 17:27.800
I know it was only your
soul, but that's just it...

17:28.480 --> 17:30.760
If I was able to pull that much of you out,

17:30.780 --> 17:34.760
then I've got a hunch that your body's
still in there, and I can pull it out.

17:35.020 --> 17:37.140
You think my body's still in the portal?

17:37.180 --> 17:39.380
Existing separately from my soul?

17:39.520 --> 17:42.120
[GASPS] Like Barry's body!

17:44.540 --> 17:46.880
Right. What did you see?

17:46.880 --> 17:48.100
Try to think back.

17:48.120 --> 17:51.020
Can you remember what happened
when the truth unraveled you?

17:54.080 --> 17:55.620
I reached out...

17:57.900 --> 17:59.260
And it was me.

17:59.260 --> 18:01.040
It was my hand I grabbed!

18:01.820 --> 18:02.820
I knew it.

18:02.820 --> 18:05.200
Doesn't look like we're
done with the truth yet, Al.

18:05.200 --> 18:07.640
We're gonna get in there
and pull your body out.

18:07.760 --> 18:09.080
Brother...

18:09.800 --> 18:14.100
AL: After the portal, I remember
looking at you from inside that thing...

18:14.180 --> 18:16.360
The thing we thought was Mom.

18:16.960 --> 18:18.980
You were inside of it?

18:19.240 --> 18:20.760
That thing was you?

18:20.820 --> 18:22.000
AL: I guess so.

18:22.000 --> 18:23.780
But my soul didn't bind.

18:23.800 --> 18:25.920
It must have rejected me right away.

18:27.080 --> 18:28.480
So that means...

18:28.520 --> 18:31.460
We didn't harm
anyone else's soul after all.

18:33.180 --> 18:34.260
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

18:34.260 --> 18:35.280
[ED AND AL GASP]

18:35.320 --> 18:39.020
Mr. Elric? You have
a telephone call from Izumi Curtis.

18:40.980 --> 18:42.780
IZUMI: I did some research.

18:42.800 --> 18:46.700
Sig and I looked up our family lines,
and well...

18:46.740 --> 18:49.960
The child that I transmuted... It couldn't...

18:50.120 --> 18:53.680
It didn't have a single physical trait
that could have come from us.

18:55.340 --> 18:57.340
You're onto something, aren't you?

18:57.360 --> 18:58.320
Yes.

18:58.520 --> 19:01.280
I've come to the conclusion
that death is permanent.

19:02.220 --> 19:05.800
So not even transmutation
can change that fact.

19:07.260 --> 19:09.220
All this time...

19:09.260 --> 19:11.980
I thought that I must have missed something.

19:11.980 --> 19:14.700
But it was impossible
to do in the first place.

19:16.720 --> 19:17.540
Ed.

19:17.540 --> 19:18.760
Yes, ma'am?!

19:20.520 --> 19:22.400
Thank you.
[LINE DISCONNECTS]

19:26.200 --> 19:28.180
AL: So what did Teacher have to say?

19:29.400 --> 19:32.660
Well, I'm not really sure why, but she said...

19:32.820 --> 19:33.840
Thank you.

19:42.880 --> 19:43.960
Al...?

19:45.680 --> 19:49.840
This entire time, I've been
blaming myself for what happened.

19:50.900 --> 19:52.720
I thought it was me.

19:53.040 --> 19:56.420
I thought I was the one who
killed Mom a second time.

19:58.320 --> 20:00.120
And so did I, Al.

20:01.280 --> 20:03.660
Thanks, brother. Thank you.

20:03.720 --> 20:06.920
I wasn't the one who killed Mom after all.

20:10.420 --> 20:11.760
Izumi...

20:12.540 --> 20:15.040
I feel like I've been brought back to life.

20:15.720 --> 20:19.520
Our child wasn't made to
suffer twice because of me.

20:22.820 --> 20:23.460
ED: But still...

20:23.460 --> 20:27.000
None of this changes the fact
that I'm the one who put you in that body.

20:27.280 --> 20:30.480
And I don't care what it takes.
I'm gonna make you normal again—

20:30.480 --> 20:31.220
Brother!

20:31.540 --> 20:34.860
I was right there with you,
and I knew that there were risks.

20:35.020 --> 20:38.040
So quit trying to shoulder
all of this on your own.

20:39.120 --> 20:41.320
I can't watch you suffer like this.

20:41.640 --> 20:43.020
Not on your own.

20:43.160 --> 20:47.080
I can't just stand back and watch
other people get hurt over what I've done.

20:47.440 --> 20:49.700
Like what happened to Mr. Hughes.

20:51.780 --> 20:55.380
I felt like it was my fault
when I found out he was dead.

20:55.780 --> 20:58.820
And I told myself that
if it meant other people getting hurt

20:58.820 --> 21:01.140
then I don't even want my body back.

21:05.160 --> 21:06.320
Brother...

21:06.580 --> 21:09.560
I've met other people
who weren't exactly human.

21:09.780 --> 21:12.840
But they still managed to
live their lives with a purpose.

21:14.100 --> 21:15.660
And even in this body...

21:15.700 --> 21:19.320
it hasn't stopped other people
from treating me like I'm still human.

21:20.040 --> 21:22.600
This body could reject me any time.

21:22.600 --> 21:24.500
But it's the same with being human.

21:24.520 --> 21:27.460
You never know when you
might get sick or die in an accident.

21:28.020 --> 21:30.080
So I can still get by like this.

21:30.480 --> 21:32.600
I can live a somewhat normal life.

21:32.860 --> 21:35.160
And that's how I've managed to keep going.

21:35.480 --> 21:36.980
But now...

21:37.340 --> 21:39.480
I can't take it anymore!

21:43.120 --> 21:46.840
Because... I can't...

21:47.760 --> 21:50.600
I can't take all the nights by myself!

21:52.820 --> 21:54.480
It's too lonely.

21:54.700 --> 21:57.280
And that's why I have
to get back to normal.

21:57.640 --> 21:59.860
Sure. And you're going to.

21:59.860 --> 22:00.880
[CLANG]

22:01.360 --> 22:03.600
We'll knock that truth jerk on his butt.

22:03.660 --> 22:06.360
And then we're gonna pull
your body right out of that place.

22:06.400 --> 22:07.620
AL: Yeah!

22:17.580 --> 22:18.720
WINRY: Huh?

22:20.600 --> 22:21.700
That's weird.

22:22.200 --> 22:25.280
Have his shoulders always been so broad?

22:28.860 --> 22:34.400
Let it all out, let it all out

22:34.400 --> 22:38.760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

22:39.760 --> 22:45.100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

22:45.100 --> 22:51.120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:51.580 --> 22:56.820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

22:56.820 --> 23:02.200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

23:02.720 --> 23:11.960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

23:12.160 --> 23:17.580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

23:17.660 --> 23:23.840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:23.840 --> 23:31.780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

23:31.780 --> 23:34.040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

23:34.040 --> 23:39.340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

23:39.340 --> 23:45.560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

23:45.560 --> 23:53.200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

23:53.440 --> 23:57.740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

24:00.740 --> 24:07.260
The meer sight of his injured friend hastens the Colonel's
determination to uncover the forces plaguing the military.

24:07.720 --> 24:10.900
While the young man is forced to
put everything he has on the line

24:10.960 --> 24:13.340
In order to escape from a dead end.

24:13.760 --> 24:17.280
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:17.700 --> 24:21.680
Episode 21: Advance of the Fool

24:22.000 --> 24:27.000
Never wait for the battle to come to you.
Strike the first blow.
